# Third-party reference material - studied, never redistributed.
#
# docs/reference/ is a default-deny home: everything inside it is ignored,
# forever, without anyone having to add a rule. Put ALL study material there -
# captures, screenshots, downloaded kits, behaviour studies, competitor UI.
#
# The named paths below are the legacy ones from before that rule existed. Do
# not add to them. Chasing filenames is how a 2.7GB kit of somebody else's
# product ended up untracked but NOT ignored, one `git add -A` away from a
# public commit that would also have named them in the directory path.
docs/reference/
docs/images/menus/
docs/images/3_main/
docs/behaviour-reference.md
docs/*-behaviour-reference.md
**/*[Rr]eference[_-][Kk]it*/
**/*reference-kit*/
# The capture kit is 2.7GB of somebody else's product, and its directory name
# names them. Matched by shape as well as by path so a rename does not re-arm it.
docs/images/*Reference_Kit*/
docs/images/**/pictures_from_the_checklist/
docs/images/**/recording_screenshots/

# Raw dictation and scratch notes - working material, not portfolio material
docs/images/justwords.txt

# Internal working notes - not portfolio material.
#
# docs/private/ is the default-deny home for these, same principle as
# docs/reference/ above. Ops notes, audits, anything that records production
# identifiers or reasoning that is not part of the public record.
#
# An ops note carrying the live database project ref sat in a public repository
# for four days before anyone noticed. It was deleted at HEAD and stayed
# readable in history for another eight.
docs/private/
docs/handoff/reference-hygiene.md
docs/handoff/migration-state.md
**/*-audit-internal.md
**/*.private.md
